  <section>
    <h2>Starting the design</h2>
    <p>I sketched several versions of each screen on paper first, so the elements that made it into the digital wireframes would address users’ pain points. For the home screen, I prioritized a layout that gives enough information without overwhelming people. Stars mark the parts of each sketch I carried into the digital wireframes.</p>
    <figure class="case-wide">{% picture "projects/petchecker/paper-wireframes.jpg", "Two notebook pages of pencil sketches labelled #1 Project for Google Class, showing five versions of the home screen, labelled A to E, with stars marking the elements chosen for the digital wireframes.", "(min-width: 72rem) 72rem, 100vw", "lazy", [900, 2048] %}</figure>
    <p>From there I built digital wireframes based on the research: a button at the top of the home screen gets you to your recommended food fast, and each screen gives a clear route and a digestible amount of information.</p>
    <div class="case-compare">
